(:id "port/python/vt/wide-scalars" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtwide_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtWideRows (every manifest instance whose unit's table closure carries fixed(I, F), ufixed(I, F), int128 or uint128: scalars_full, scalars_default, scalars_edges as form 3, widelist_wide as form 1; the selection comes from ir.TableWideFields and must cover both declared forms)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/vtwide_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtWideRowsNegativeControl/uint128-width, /fixed-wide-width (each fault planted in a COPY of the emitted runtime: kind_int.py's uint128 width and fixedform.py's 128-bit read width; each control requires every row it names red)" "make python-vt-wide-rows python-vt-wide-rows-negative-control (make/python-vt-wide-rows.mk); make/negative-controls.d/python-vt-wide-rows-negative-control.json: python-vt-wide-rows-negative-control") :tested-revision "14525c669f10c70181268462633dd13c1bd9964b" :note "2026-11-17: the wide-scalars row on the Python table leg. Every manifest instance whose unit carries a wide scalar is read once and written back byte-identical to the canonical wire, with measure equal to the saved length and the loaded value unchanged by the save, under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 from make dist-python); scalars_full, scalars_default and scalars_edges are a fixed-declared root read as form 3 through the generated fixed form, and widelist_wide is a variable root read as form 1. A wire-refused instance, had the corpus named one, is held to its refusal with the caller's bytearray untouched. The report rows in the same units (scalars_full_as_2, scalars_edges_as_2, field_scalar_widen and the previous-form rows) are the widening cell's and are not held here. The negative control turns the uint128 width off in a copy of kind_int.py (widelist_wide red under both pins) and cuts the fixed form's 128-bit read to 8 bytes in a copy of fixedform.py (scalars_full and scalars_edges red under both pins); scalars_default is not guarded by that control, since every 128-bit value in it (reach, mass, flux and entity_id 0, energy its default -250) fits in 64 bits and the 8-byte read gives the same value. Run on macOS arm64 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 and -tags schema_leg_python; the same head passed make generated-current. No hot path changed, so no bench row moved; the wide kinds ride the integer codec the table core bench already measures.")
